  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">First published as a smaller artist anthology: Wind blown cloud. [Edinburgh : Morning Star ; Newcastle-upon-Tyne : Baltic, 2002].</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Originally inspired by the seventeenth-century Japanese poet Basho's The road to the far north, with its beautiful description of being"drawn like a wind blown cloud" on a wandering spring journey--Jacket.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">A collection forming part of The Archive of Wind Blown Clouds. The Archive, Of f Quay Building, Foundry Lane, Byker, Newcastle-upon-Tyne NE6 1LH.  Director: Alec Finlay; archivist, Laura Harrington.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Includes index of poems.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Poetic and stunning cloud images from people all over the world--Gwangju, Punta del Este, Kinloch Rannoch--from photographers young and old, experienced and amateur; huffs of white cloud, storm masses, bold sunsets, reflections, and skyscapes with a selection of classical Japanese and western haiku.</subfield>
  </datafield>
